# E-D4-03 pins (D4, P4-4-S2), read by run.sh. Every pin here is a first-use
# pin: D4 read each digest or hash on 2026-11-11 from the source named, and
# no upstream publishes a signature for these artifacts (the note, section 2).
#
# Zeek 9.0.1, the `lts` tag on 2026-11-11, linux/amd64 manifest, from Docker
# Hub's tag listing for zeek/zeek (the Zeek project's official repository).
ZEEK_IMAGE=zeek/zeek@sha256:71c1d6b61cdcc25d306c091d32b3da15583485c0c9dfc45cdff48b088cdfdc92
ZEEK_VERSION="zeek version 9.0.1"
# Suricata 8.0.8, linux/amd64 manifest, from Docker Hub's tag listing for
# jasonish/suricata. It is a personal account, not an OISF organisation one:
# an image OISF does not publish, accepted for this comparison only and never
# in a sensor (D1 on #625). Suricata is the comparison, not the choice (D1 on
# #637; D7's N5 on #637).
SURICATA_IMAGE=jasonish/suricata@sha256:a8277a84662969927de6bf6fd1848f64f353e47dd498d1b7d11f75b89096be1f
SURICATA_VERSION="This is Suricata version 8.0.8 RELEASE"
# ICSNPP packages: scripts only, no plugin to build. Fetched file by file at
# these commits and checked against icsnpp.sha256 before Zeek loads them.
ICSNPP_DNP3_COMMIT=b31dbadeceb1cbcda16aef89c650559cd177dd7e
ICSNPP_MODBUS_COMMIT=6dd3dab173169e454a73925d0426d3c019104852
# D6's pass conditions as reviewed and merged with #623 (main 96c35ef8, LF
# endings). Not a first-use pin: the file is the project's own. A run counts
# only on main with this file at this hash (the tables' header).
CONDITIONS_SHA256=38e6c081c7ab62b2b88e8bef1574d136121a3a839f4499d6fe8ba7d7e8acc80e
# P4-4-E2 (D4-90): D6's pass conditions for the Modbus signature,
# tests/integration/gt_pcap/modbus-signature-conditions.tsv, as merged with
# #642 (main 799de090, LF endings), under the name D6 gave the pin. Not a
# first-use pin: the file is the project's own.
MODBUS_SIGNATURE_CONDITIONS_SHA256=7b242b85a3387c3f591eb21cce2e3f036feb8c1c8799e02857548a2e5f6f4418
# The corpus's manifest and its labels, tests/fixtures/network/
# modbus-sig-corpus/corpus.tsv and labels.tsv (LF endings), D4's, pinned
# before the counted run (D6's corpus-pins). A run of P4-4-E2 counts only
# from main with these four files at their pins (D6's judge-counted).
MODBUS_SIG_CORPUS_SHA256=
MODBUS_SIG_LABELS_SHA256=
